we run up against human nature

258
00:12:42,320 --> 00:12:45,000
and we either roll with the punches or we punch back,

259
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:46,440
and if we punch back,

260
00:12:46,440 --> 00:12:49,960
human nature counter punches us a little harder sometimes.

261
00:12:49,960 --> 00:12:51,840
Now I know some folks would disagree,

262
00:12:51,840 --> 00:12:53,160
but I think you're right.

263
00:12:53,160 --> 00:12:55,520
We ought not to make scouts suffer

264
00:12:55,520 --> 00:12:57,400
for things they can't control,

265
00:12:57,400 --> 00:12:59,800
and they can't control what their parents are gonna do

266
00:12:59,800 --> 00:13:02,080
when it comes to turning forms in right,

267
00:13:02,080 --> 00:13:03,480
I bet every single troop

268
00:13:03,480 --> 00:13:05,800
that's listening to the podcast right now

269
00:13:05,800 --> 00:13:08,360
has a deadline for permission slips

270
00:13:08,360 --> 00:13:10,000
that is rigidly flexible.

271
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:11,120
I know we do.

272
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:12,940
I think we want a permission slip,

273
00:13:12,940 --> 00:13:15,560
as you suggested, like two weeks ahead.

274
00:13:15,560 --> 00:13:18,040
but we also understand human nature

275
00:13:18,040 --> 00:13:19,840
and people do what people do

276
00:13:19,840 --> 00:13:21,680
and we'd rather have a scout go camping

277
00:13:21,680 --> 00:13:22,640
than have them sit at home

278
00:13:22,640 --> 00:13:24,920
because of a piece of paper.

279
00:13:24,920 --> 00:13:26,380
So, understanding, Craig,

280
00:13:26,380 --> 00:13:29,440
that this is kind of a non-answer answer,

281
00:13:29,440 --> 00:13:32,560
I don't really have a solution for you.

282
00:13:32,560 --> 00:13:34,680
Let's ask everybody out there

283
00:13:34,720 --> 00:13:36,480
if what they do

284
00:13:36,480 --> 00:13:38,560
as far as permission slips and deadlines

285
00:13:38,560 --> 00:13:39,400
and things like that

286
00:13:39,400 --> 00:13:42,540
are folks tell me about any successful practices

287
00:13:42,540 --> 00:13:46,120
that you've had that seem to help out with this problem.

288
00:13:46,120 --> 00:13:47,680
I'm sure everybody understands

289
00:13:47,680 --> 00:13:49,440
exactly what the problem is.

290
00:13:49,440 --> 00:13:53,220
Get in touch with me at Clark at scoutmastercgcom

291
00:13:53,220 --> 00:13:56,320
and let me know if you've got a better answer for Craig.

292
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:57,560
I heard from Steve who said

293
00:13:57,560 --> 00:13:58,920
I have three new scouts

294
00:13:58,920 --> 00:14:00,760
who've just crossed over from Weebelos

295
00:14:00,760 --> 00:14:03,680
and they are planning to attend summer camp.

296
00:14:03,680 --> 00:14:06,240
Our camp is four and a half hours away.

297
00:14:06,240 --> 00:14:08,200
I'm prepared for everything,

298
00:14:08,200 --> 00:14:13,120
I think, except possible bouts of homesickness.

299
00:14:13,120 --> 00:14:15,400
Do you have any articles you can suggest?

300
00:14:15,400 --> 00:14:17,080
It would be greatly appreciated.

301
00:14:17,080 --> 00:14:18,600
Steve, I do.

302
00:14:18,600 --> 00:14:20,640
I have a couple of articles

303
00:14:20,640 --> 00:14:22,820
about dealing with homesickness.

304
00:14:22,820 --> 00:14:26,240
I won't go into every single detail here,

305
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:27,760
but hitting the high points.

306
00:14:27,760 --> 00:14:30,200
Homesickness is not uncommon.

307
00:14:30,200 --> 00:14:33,400
It's not a fair complete either.

308
00:14:33,400 --> 00:14:35,079
just because a younger scout

309
00:14:35,079 --> 00:14:36,880
is going to travel a distance

310
00:14:36,880 --> 00:14:38,280
and go to a week of summer camp

311
00:14:38,280 --> 00:14:40,760
doesn't immediately mean

312
00:14:40,760 --> 00:14:42,680
that you would expect them to be homesick.

313
00:14:42,680 --> 00:14:45,880
But naturally you want to be prepared if they are.

314
00:14:45,880 --> 00:14:48,319
And you'll find, if you take a look at these articles-

315
00:14:48,319 --> 00:14:49,500
and I'll have a link to them

316
00:14:49,500 --> 00:14:51,640
in the post that contains this podcast-

317
00:14:51,640 --> 00:14:52,980
that there are some strategies

318
00:14:52,980 --> 00:14:55,520
that parents can use ahead of time

319
00:14:55,520 --> 00:14:58,480
If they suspect their scout might be homesick

320
00:14:58,480 --> 00:14:59,380
while they're away from home.

321
00:14:59,380 --> 00:15:02,120
there's some strategies parents can apply ahead of time.

322
00:15:02,120 --> 00:15:04,600
More about this particular thing

323
00:15:04,600 --> 00:15:07,560
ends up in the hands of parents

324
00:15:07,560 --> 00:15:08,920
than it does of scouts.

325
00:15:08,920 --> 00:15:10,040
If you read these articles

326
00:15:10,040 --> 00:15:14,160
I also have some very specific strategies for scouts

327
00:15:14,160 --> 00:15:16,920
to employ if they encounter homesickness.

328
00:15:16,920 --> 00:15:17,760
But with homesickness

329
00:15:17,760 --> 00:15:20,320
an ounce of prevention is worth a pound of cure.

330
00:15:20,320 --> 00:15:22,400
So you want to review that,

331
00:15:22,400 --> 00:15:25,320
share that information with the parents of your scouts

332
00:15:25,320 --> 00:15:28,320
and get them utilizing some of those strategies

333
00:15:28,320 --> 00:15:29,880
that are explained in those articles

334
00:15:29,880 --> 00:15:31,400
And that way you'll get to summer camp

335
00:15:31,400 --> 00:15:34,319
and hopefully you won't have any bouts of homesickness

336
00:15:34,319 --> 00:15:35,920
and everybody will have a great time.

337
00:15:35,920 --> 00:15:38,120
Here's an interesting question from Bob.

338
00:15:38,120 --> 00:15:42,260
Where do you put merit badges on the uniform without a sash?

339
00:15:42,260 --> 00:15:44,480
Well, it's a pretty easy answer:

340
00:15:44,480 --> 00:15:47,600
Go to the guide to awards and insignia

341
00:15:47,600 --> 00:15:49,880
and I'll have a link to a PDF version of that

342
00:15:49,880 --> 00:15:52,160
on the post that contains this podcast

343
00:15:52,160 --> 00:15:54,319
And on page 31,

344
00:15:54,319 --> 00:15:58,199
you will see an illustration of where merit badges

345
00:15:58,199 --> 00:15:59,920
can go on the scout uniform.

346
00:15:59,920 --> 00:16:03,400
It's on the right sleeve in what is called position four.

347
00:16:03,400 --> 00:16:05,880
It's limited to six merit badges.

348
00:16:05,880 --> 00:16:08,720
Now it'll only work on a long-sleeved uniform shirt,

349
00:16:08,720 --> 00:16:10,560
Otherwise you'll have to get a sash.

350
00:16:10,560 --> 00:16:12,000
But I hope that helps. Bob

351
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:14,280
Had a question from Greg Gotcher,

352
00:16:14,280 --> 00:16:18,520
who is with Troop 372 in Waterford, Wisconsin,

353
00:16:18,520 --> 00:16:19,360
And Greg said

354
00:16:19,360 --> 00:16:22,600
I followed five weeblos into a Boy Scout Troop

355
00:16:22,600 --> 00:16:25,120
and they've asked me to become the new scout master.

356
00:16:25,120 --> 00:16:26,920
So into the volcano I go.

357
00:16:26,920 --> 00:16:28,100
Well, good for you, Greg.

358
00:16:28,100 --> 00:16:30,580
I'm really excited to see a transition

359
00:16:30,580 --> 00:16:32,420
into a patrol based Troop.

360
00:16:32,420 --> 00:16:35,180
Our first activity was this past weekend.

361
00:16:35,180 --> 00:16:36,540
We were out camping with the Troop

362
00:16:36,540 --> 00:16:39,220
and I was encouraged to see that it's somewhere

363
00:16:39,220 --> 00:16:42,220
in the middle of adult lead and scout lead

364
00:16:42,220 --> 00:16:45,780
and leaning closer to the scout lead side of things.

365
00:16:45,780 --> 00:16:49,020
So I'm encouraged at taking over as a new scout master.

366
00:16:49,020 --> 00:16:52,140
but I have a few questions about youth leadership.

367
00:16:52,140 --> 00:16:55,620
Well, Greg, it sounds like you're having a great time.

368
00:16:55,620 --> 00:16:57,460
Let's see if we can answer your questions.

369
00:16:57,460 --> 00:16:59,900
So Greg's first question was:

370
00:16:59,900 --> 00:17:02,060
is the senior patrol leader

371
00:17:02,060 --> 00:17:06,100
and the assistant senior patrol leader part of a patrol?

372
00:17:06,100 --> 00:17:08,740
Well, Greg, if you look in the scout master's handbook,

373
00:17:08,740 --> 00:17:10,900
you'll see that the senior patrol leader

374
00:17:10,900 --> 00:17:14,220
and assistant senior patrol leader are not patrol members.

375
00:17:14,220 --> 00:17:16,300
Now, there's really not a definitive statement

376
00:17:16,300 --> 00:17:18,220
that I could find when I was looking

377
00:17:18,220 --> 00:17:20,819
about the senior patrol leader status,

378
00:17:20,819 --> 00:17:22,060
But it does say this:

379
00:17:22,060 --> 00:17:25,500
during his tenure as assistant senior patrol leader,

380
00:17:25,540 --> 00:17:28,260
the scout is not a member of a patrol.

381
00:17:28,260 --> 00:17:29,540
Greg goes on to ask:

382
00:17:29,540 --> 00:17:32,860
are there any other positions of responsibility

383
00:17:32,860 --> 00:17:34,660
that aren't part of a patrol?

384
00:17:34,660 --> 00:17:35,740
Well, at, once again

385
00:17:35,740 --> 00:17:37,540
looking in the scout master's handbook,

386
00:17:37,540 --> 00:17:38,780
it says scouts serving

387
00:17:38,780 --> 00:17:41,140
in any of the following troop positions.

388
00:17:41,140 --> 00:17:43,940
then it goes on to list all of the positions

389
00:17:43,940 --> 00:17:45,940
of responsibility within a troop,

390
00:17:45,940 --> 00:17:49,860
like scribe, quarter, master, things like that-

391
00:17:49,860 --> 00:17:53,660
will also continue to be active members of their patrols.

392
00:17:53,700 --> 00:17:55,500
So other than the senior patrol leader

393
00:17:55,500 --> 00:17:57,020
and assistant senior patrol leader,

394
00:17:57,020 --> 00:17:59,380
everybody with a position of responsibility

395
00:17:59,380 --> 00:18:01,220
is still an active member of their patrol.

396
00:18:01,220 --> 00:18:02,180
Greg then asks:

397
00:18:02,180 --> 00:18:04,380
so if the senior patrol leader

398
00:18:04,380 --> 00:18:06,300
and assistant senior patrol leader

399
00:18:06,300 --> 00:18:07,860
aren't members of a patrol,

400
00:18:07,860 --> 00:18:10,620
are they not participating in any patrol activities?

401
00:18:10,620 --> 00:18:13,020
And I think that depends, Greg.

402
00:18:13,020 --> 00:18:14,580
If they're invited to participate

403
00:18:14,580 --> 00:18:16,340
by the patrol, they certainly could,

404
00:18:16,340 --> 00:18:17,940
But just the nature of things,

405
00:18:17,940 --> 00:18:19,940
I wouldn't see them as being participants

406
00:18:19,940 --> 00:18:21,460
on the same level as a member,

407
00:18:21,460 --> 00:18:23,420
where they're expected to be there all the time

408
00:18:23,420 --> 00:18:25,980
or to be a part of the patrol team.

409
00:18:25,980 --> 00:18:27,220
They're gonna have their hands full

410
00:18:27,220 --> 00:18:28,860
and they'll interact with the patrols

411
00:18:28,860 --> 00:18:30,580
and the scouts a whole lot.

412
00:18:30,580 --> 00:18:33,460
So whether or not they're a formal member or not,

413
00:18:33,460 --> 00:18:37,340
I don't think that makes a great deal of difference.

414
00:18:37,340 --> 00:18:40,940
And Greg brings up one very practical question.

415
00:18:40,940 --> 00:18:42,980
So do the assistant senior patrol leader

416
00:18:42,980 --> 00:18:45,580
and senior patrol leader can't by themselves

417
00:18:45,580 --> 00:18:47,620
and do their own cooking and things like that?

418
00:18:47,620 --> 00:18:51,380
Well, I think that they could if they wanted to.

419
00:18:51,380 --> 00:18:53,340
I know that our tradition has been

420
00:18:53,340 --> 00:18:55,699
that our senior patrol leader and his assistant camp

421
00:18:55,699 --> 00:18:57,340
and cook along with the adults

422
00:18:57,340 --> 00:18:59,100
seems to work out pretty good for us,

423
00:18:59,100 --> 00:19:01,020
And the scouts who occupy those positions

424
00:19:01,020 --> 00:19:02,899
of responsibility don't seem to mind.

425
00:19:02,899 --> 00:19:04,459
I'd be curious to know if people

426
00:19:04,459 --> 00:19:06,260
who do that any differently anywhere,

427
00:19:06,260 --> 00:19:09,100
but one of my aims in that arrangement

428
00:19:09,100 --> 00:19:11,300
is keeping them out of the patrol campsite

429
00:19:11,300 --> 00:19:13,820
so that they don't become the default patrol leader.

430
00:19:13,820 --> 00:19:16,419
And then the final question that Greg asked:

431
00:19:16,419 --> 00:19:18,080
how do you see all this working

432
00:19:18,080 --> 00:19:20,179
for a group of 16 boys?

433
00:19:20,179 --> 00:19:22,500
Well, I think it's gonna work just fine.

434
00:19:22,500 --> 00:19:24,980
Of the 16, two won't be members of a patrol,

435
00:19:24,980 --> 00:19:27,020
So you have 14 scouts remaining.

436
00:19:27,020 --> 00:19:28,580
That sounds like a planning

437
00:19:28,580 --> 00:19:30,540
for two really good, strong patrols.

438
00:19:30,540 --> 00:19:33,140
Now I say two, but you might end up with three,

439
00:19:33,140 --> 00:19:33,980
You don't know.

440
00:19:33,980 --> 00:19:36,460
Let's see what the scouts wanna work out

441
00:19:36,460 --> 00:19:38,160
so far as setting up their patrols.

442
00:19:38,160 --> 00:19:39,980
So when that question comes up,

443
00:19:39,980 --> 00:19:42,160
don't answer that question for them.

444
00:19:42,160 --> 00:19:44,380
Put that question to the patrol leaders council

445
00:19:44,380 --> 00:19:45,860
and say: how do you wanna set this up

446
00:19:45,860 --> 00:19:47,260
And see what they have to say.

447
00:19:47,260 --> 00:19:49,100
We'll give them our best advice

448
00:19:49,100 --> 00:19:52,060
on what makes a workable patrol and things like that.

449
00:19:52,060 --> 00:19:53,179
Let's see what they come up with.

450
00:19:53,179 --> 00:19:55,139
Let's see what answers they have.

451
00:19:55,139 --> 00:19:57,899
So, Greg, I hope those answers helped you out a little bit,

452
00:19:57,899 --> 00:20:00,580
and congratulations on jumping into the volcano here

453
00:20:00,580 --> 00:20:01,500
with the rest of us.

